\title{MRKCFC: Multivariate Robust K-Centers Functional Clustering for Sparsely Observed Longitudinal Data}
\description{
Multivariate K-centers functional clustering (MKCFC) and its robust form (MRKCFC) for sparsely and irregularly observed multivariate longitudinal data that may be non-Gaussian. Each class is described by a two-stage multivariate functional principal component analysis, a marginal analysis of each variable followed by an eigendecomposition of the stacked scores, and subjects are reassigned to the class that reconstructs their trajectories best. The robust form uses Kendall's tau functional principal component analysis in the first stage and a spatial-sign scatter matrix in the second, so that neither stage needs a moment assumption on the principal component scores. The package also carries the cluster-validity criteria, metrics and data-generating functions used by the accompanying manuscript; the study scripts that call them are distributed separately \url{https://github.com/BingbingFan/MRKCFC_Simulation}. Includes an internal KFPCA-derived implementation based on KFPCA version 2.0 by Rou Zhong and Jingxiao Zhang \url{https://github.com/BingbingFan/KFPCA}, incorporated under GPL (>= 3). MRKCFC-specific adaptations are by Bingbing Fan and are identified in the source.
